{"id":"6f15a303-c850-4972-b133-4aa60cedd1c2","createdAt":"2026-10-26T14:35:54.793Z","batchId":"profile_claude-opus-5-5_low","approach":"html","modelId":"claude-opus-5-5","settings":{"effort":"low"},"presetId":"profile","prompt":"A user profile card with avatar, name, role, short bio, a few stats and a follow button.","system":"Return only the body content of an HTML page: no doctype, <html>, <head> or <body> tags, no markdown, no code fences, no prose. The page shell below is already loaded, so build with its classes and chart helper. Inline <script> is allowed for interactivity (tabs, toggles, filters); no external requests. Add a small <style> block only for what the classes cannot express, or when the request asks for a different look, colours, fonts or layout: then follow the request.\nPAGE SHELL (already loaded; do not restate it):\n- A stylesheet with these classes. Use them instead of writing CSS:\n  layout: page (centered column), stack, row, between, center, gap-sm, gap-lg, grid + cols-2|cols-3|cols-4 (responsive)\n  surfaces: card, card-title, card-desc, alert, alert-destructive, hr\n  text: h1-h4 (styled), lead, muted, small, up, down (trend colours)\n  controls: btn, btn-secondary|btn-outline|btn-ghost|btn-destructive, btn-sm|btn-lg, btn-block; label wraps input/select/textarea; label.check wraps a checkbox or radio\n  data: table (styled; td.num for numbers), badge, badge-secondary|badge-outline|badge-destructive, stat-label, stat-value, progress (inner div with style=\"width:NN%\"), avatar\n- Charts: <div data-chart='{\"type\":\"bar|line|area|pie\",\"title\":\"…\",\"data\":[{\"label\":\"W1\",\"value\":120}]}'></div> renders an SVG chart (single series, pie gets a legend). Do not draw charts yourself.\n- Light and dark mode are handled by the stylesheet.\n\nDESIGN BRIEF (applies to every UI you produce):\n- Build a complete, realistic screen, not a skeleton: a clear title and intro, grouped sections, and enough detail that it could ship.\n- Cover exactly what the request names, with no extra pages or marketing sections.\n- Use the supplied DATA in full: every field is there to be shown. Derive useful extras from it (shares, totals, deltas, rankings) instead of inventing unrelated numbers.\n- Where it fits, add status badges, trend/change figures, secondary actions, helper text, and sensible empty or edge-case copy.\n- Establish hierarchy with headings, size and weight; group related items; keep spacing and alignment consistent.\n- Make charts readable: a title, labelled axes or values, and a legend for pie charts.\n- Never use lorem ipsum or placeholder names like \"Item 1\".","systemHash":"0c16911c9564c3db3ada7a622931ee6ffc820ebf9a373996782a9f1f0fc3c98c","systemOverridden":false,"strictOutput":false,"rawOutput":"<div class=\"page stack gap-lg\">\n  <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n    <h1 class=\"h1\">Profile</h1>\n    <p class=\"lead muted\">See who's behind the work, and follow along for new projects and writing.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"card stack gap-lg\" style=\"max-width:520px\">\n    <div class=\"row gap-lg\" style=\"align-items:center\">\n      <div class=\"avatar\" style=\"width:72px;height:72px;font-size:1.5rem\">MO</div>\n      <div class=\"stack gap-sm\" style=\"flex:1\">\n        <div class=\"row gap-sm\" style=\"align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap\">\n          <h2 class=\"h3\" style=\"margin:0\">Maya Okafor</h2>\n          <span class=\"badge\">Verified</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"muted\" style=\"margin:0\">Senior Product Designer · Lumen Health</p>\n        <p class=\"small muted\" style=\"margin:0\">Lisbon, Portugal · Joined March 2019</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <p style=\"margin:0\">Designing calmer healthcare tools for clinicians and patients. I write about design systems and accessibility, and mentor early-career designers on weekends.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"row gap-sm\" style=\"flex-wrap:wrap\">\n      <span class=\"badge badge-secondary\">Design systems</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge-secondary\">Accessibility</span>\n      <span class=\"badge badge-secondary\">Prototyping</span>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"hr\"></div>\n\n    <div class=\"grid cols-3\">\n      <div class=\"stack\">\n        <span class=\"stat-label\">Projects</span>\n        <span class=\"stat-value\">48</span>\n        <span class=\"small up\">+6 this year</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"stack\">\n        <span class=\"stat-label\">Followers</span>\n        <span class=\"stat-value\" id=\"followers\">12,480</span>\n        <span class=\"small up\">+3.2% this month</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"stack\">\n        <span class=\"stat-label\">Following</span>\n        <span class=\"stat-value\">312</span>\n        <span class=\"small muted\">Since 2019</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"row gap-sm\">\n      <button class=\"btn\" id=\"followBtn\" style=\"flex:1\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Follow</button>\n      <button class=\"btn btn-outline\">Message</button>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"small muted\" id=\"followHint\" style=\"margin:0\">Follow to get updates when Maya shares new work.</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var btn=document.getElementById('followBtn'),\n      count=document.getElementById('followers'),\n      hint=document.getElementById('followHint'),\n      base=12480, following=false;\n  btn.addEventListener('click',function(){\n    following=!following;\n    btn.textContent=following?'Following':'Follow';\n    btn.className=following?'btn btn-secondary':'btn';\n    btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed',following);\n    count.textContent=(base+(following?1:0)).toLocaleString();\n    hint.textContent=following?'You\\'ll see Maya\\'s new projects in your feed. Click again to unfollow.':'Follow to get updates when Maya shares new work.';\n  });\n})();\n</script>","deltas":[[1708,"<div class=\"page st"],[1729,"ack g"],[1810,"ap-lg\">\n  <"],[1855,"div class=\"stack gap-"],[1908,"sm\">\n    <h1"